rect-t1-decline — REFUTED. #472's t=1 cost is NOT the rectangle code path.
================================================================================

Date        2026-08-09
Host        Apple M4 Pro (8P + 4E, 12 logical), macOS 26.5.2, idle box
Base        main @ cebb97f
Branch      perf/rect-t1-decline  (main + `git merge fix/rect-rowview` + the gate)
Data        benchmarks/rect_t1_decline_gap_2026-08-09.tsv   (288 rows, foreign_max = 0 on ALL of them)
Reference   dav1d 1.5.4, `--framedelay 1`, measured in the SAME interleaved sweep
Instrument  scripts/perf/verify_gap.sh, two-point wall fit at 2 and 20 frames,
            rotating arm order, strict idle gate (3 cell-rounds discarded and re-run),
            n = 9 complete rounds, no `nice` on any timed run, no -C target-cpu=native

THE HYPOTHESIS
--------------
#472 (the sound strided-rectangle record) wins big at t>1 and regresses 8bpc
t=1 from main's 1.285x to 1.320x, losing the campaign's only cell under the
~1.30x bar. #469's verification round priced that as "+0.71 ns on every
surviving registration while removing ZERO registrations", and the reasoning was
that the per-row split the rectangle collapses only exists once
`tile_threading_active()` latches — so at t=1 the rectangle can only add cost.

Predicted composite from declining the rectangle at t=1: 1.285 / 1.418 / 1.417 / 1.575.

