**Declining the rectangle at t=1 buys NOTHING (8bpc t=1 paired 1.0005) and costs
1.1% at 10bpc t=1 (the extra monotone-latch load in the predicate).** The whole of
#472's t=1 regression is still there with the rectangle path provably dead.

WHAT THAT MEANS, AND WHAT IS NOW RULED OUT
------------------------------------------
The +0.71 ns/registration is NOT paid by the rectangle. It is paid by every
registration, including the plain hull ones the rectangle never touches. Ruled
out, each with its measurement:

  * the rectangle CODE PATH (`rect_as`/`mut_rect_as` + `DisjointMutRect::row`
    per row in place of one flat guard) — this round, paired 1.0005 at 8bpc t=1
    with a `#[cfg(test)]` branch counter proving the path is dead;
  * the per-`alloc` COLUMN STORES — #472's own `cols_ab` A/B (0.9966 / 1.0139 /
    1.0037 at n=9, every band overlapping, sign inconsistent);
  * the ROW MAP being consulted on the hot path — by inspection, not by timing:
    `tracker_shard.rs`'s `add` dispatches `self.mask == 0` FIRST and returns
    before `self.rowmap.enabled()` is read, and every instance is `mask == 0`
    when no parallelism has been declared (`SHARDS_SERIAL == 1`).

What is left, and NOT measured here: `add`'s two EXTRA PARAMETERS. #469 changed
`add<IS_MUT>(&self, bounds)` into `add<IS_MUT>(&self, bounds, row_w: u32,
rows: u32)`, and `add_mut`/`add_immut` pass `0, 0`. That is two extra arguments
materialised on 7,924,706 calls per frame at t=1, on a path whose own comments
price the CALL BARRIER at 4% of the tracker and describe it as latency-bound.
The obvious test — a separate 1-argument `add_flat` for the non-rect entry
points — was NOT run, and it has a known trap: an earlier attempt to duplicate
this body for a different reason cost +0.9% on I-cache alone
(`benchmarks/tracker_borrowcost_2026-08-08.tsv`, arm `fold`).

Also worth carrying: **main measures 1.306 at 8bpc t=1 here, not 1.285.**
1.285 is #475's figure on base ee07b00; this is cebb97f on the same box. The
band [310.9..325.2] is 4.4% wide — the widest of any cell in this sweep — so
t=1 sub-2% claims on this vector need the paired statistic, not the medians.

VERDICT
-------
Do not merge the decline. Kept on the branch as the record, with its gates.

GATES
